{
  "_why": "Hand-curated doctrine vocabulary, indexed as lookup keys REGARDLESS OF FREQUENCY. Frequency mining finds what a document repeats, which in a scanned law review is the publisher's footer - it found 'electronic copy available' and missed 'spendthrift'. A term of art can appear once and still be the thing somebody looks up. Edit this file; no code change is needed.",
  "_rule": "A seed term is indexed if it APPEARS in a section. It is never invented: a term absent from the text is absent from the index, so this widens what can be found and never widens what is claimed.",
